To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Perl program to add accounts from the command line.
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96075323306819

Since there has be interest recently about adding accounts from
a command line, I decided to clean up my own perl routine the will
allow you do this, and give it out. It is a program written in
perl that takes the following arguements. Username, lastname, firstname,
group, password. The program does it's own encryption of the password,
so you do not have to type it twice. It is also fully compatible with
enhanced security. This script works for me, but keep in mind, I wrote
it for my own use, but tried to keep it very generic. Bottom line, use
at your own risk, I'm not responsible for any problems. Look over
the code for yourself, so you understand what it will do..

If you want a copy, send me email..

-- Brian
