Subject: Help - Modem problems with Gopher and Lynx (WARNING LONG)
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96075323306794

Since installing Digital UNIX V3.2b we've been having problems with the 
some modem connections.  The problem is that in lynx and gopher the arrow 
key (and I assume many other escape sequenecs) are not working.  People 
press the "down arrow" key and get ^[B instead of moving down a line.  I 
hope someone can shed some light on this for me or I'll have to spend 
money to have Digital TRY to help me.  The same connections still work 
fine on our other OSF/1 V2.0 systems.

The connections with problems seem be only modem connections that come 
through a Penril-Datability Terminal server on their way to the UNIX 
system.  Terminals connected directly to the terminal server are fine, 
but modems (with CTS/RTS flow control) have the problem.  Modems (with 
XON/XOFF flow control) connected to a DECserver 200/MC are fine.

I did an 'stty -a' and it shows that the only difference between a 
working connection and non working one is on V3.2b is:
      Works                      Doesn't Work
      ----------------           ------------
      speed 19200 baud           speed 0 baud
      clocal                     -clocal

The only differences between the connection that does not work on V3.2b 
and the same connection on V2.0 is:
      Desn't Work on V3.2b       Works on V2.0
      --------------------       ----------------
      speed 0 baud               speed 38400 baud


I'm no guru so any help would be appreciated!


