The gist of the matter is that the DEClaser 2200 is of type ln06 and not lpf,
as Phil Krause <phil@wolf.ncat.edu> and Murat Balci <balci@baum01.ege.edu.tr> 
kindly pointed out. Also the device file I was using (/dev/tty00) was incorrect, 
it should have been /dev/ttyd1. Here's a copy of the working /etc/printcap file:

lp|lp0|0|lp|laser|phil:\
        :af=/usr/adm/lpacct:\
        :br#9600:\
        :ct=dev:\
        :fc#0177777:\
        :fs#03:\
        :if=/usr/lbin/ln06rof:\
        :lf=/usr/adm/lperr:\
        :lp=/dev/ttyd1:\
        :mc#20:\
        :mx#0:\
        :of=/usr/lbin/ln06rof:\
        :pl#66:\
        :pw#80:\
        :rw:\
        :sd=/usr/spool/lpd:\
        :xc#0177777:\
        :xf=/usr/lbin/xf:\
        :xs#044000:

Once again, thanks to those who replied.

Regards Phil Sloan (sloanp@netview.shorts.co.uk)

	

