From tru64-unix-managers  Mon Sep 18 15:45:00 1995
From: "Bennett, Eric Mr." <Bennett () fsc ! vafb ! af ! mil>
Date: Mon, 18 Sep 1995 15:45:00 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY - Sendmail Aliasing for user@domain
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96075323306621


The question was how to use aliases file to get a user@domain address to 
resolve at a site where user@host.domain was the rule.

Thanks to Stephen Campbell, Andrew Gilles, Paul Rockwell, and Lucein Hercaud 
for their prompt and , in all four cases, correct and useful responses.

I inserted a MX record in the db file that the named uses pointing to the 
machine I wanted the mail delivered to.
Inserted the line    R$-<@$N>$*    $@$1<@$w>$2    user@domain
in rule S7 in the sendmail.cf file.
Then used the alises file in var/adm/sendmail to point to a real persons 
machine.

There were some other variations but this one seemed the easiest and 
quickest to do.

